{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require schools in England to allow black trainers as acceptable school footwear",
        "additional_details": "Parents should be able to choose affordable, comfortable footwear for their children. Pupils walk long distances and have different foot shapes, disabilities and individual needs. Formal shoes can cause discomfort, while vegan families may struggle to find suitable options. Foot-health guidance recommends flexible, well-fitted shoes that allow movement. The Government should require schools in England to allow safe, plain black trainers, with reasonable rules on colour, cleanliness and logos.",
        "background": "We believe the Government should update its school uniform guidance so that schools in England must allow pupils to wear plain black trainers, provided they are safe, appropriately fitted and suitable for their purpose.",
